; Preamble: run this in AutoCAD before every corpus script, in a new drawing from acadiso.dwt.
; It puts the system variables the corpus depends on into a known state. The go-draw harness does
; not run it; it sets SnapOn=false and Ortho=false on a fresh session instead (README.md).
; Lines marked (verify) name variables to be confirmed in a real install.
; no dialogs: file and command prompts come to the command line
FILEDIA
0
CMDDIA
0
; dynamic input off: typed coordinates are absolute, no tooltips take the input
DYNMODE
0
OSMODE
0
ORTHOMODE
0
SNAPMODE
0
GRIDMODE
0
POLARMODE
0
PICKFIRST
1
PICKADD
2
FILLETRAD
0
CHAMFERA
0
CHAMFERB
0
CIRCLERAD
0
OFFSETDIST
-1
COPYMODE
0
PLINEWID
0
; Standard TRIM and EXTEND: ask for cutting edges and boundaries first (2021+ default is Quick) (verify name)
TRIMEXTENDMODE
0
TRIMMODE
1
CECOLOR
BYLAYER
